# Fixed defect 120 (panel 181, 2026-09-28). Symptom: `total = base` over
# `- fee` at one margin was refused with `discarded_value`, whose fix, tagged
# `certain`, wrote `_ = - fee`; applied with `check --apply`, the program
# printed 100 where the subtraction meant 93. Cause: the lexer ended the
# first line, which can end, and the second became a statement of its own,
# whose one repair on offer kept the bug. A `-` set apart from its operand
# can only go on with the line above, so the line is refused as the break it
# is, once, and the fix writes the subtraction on one line.

function main()
    base: i64 = 100
    fee: i64 = 7
    total = base
    - fee  #~ continuation_outside_brackets
    print(total)
